00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:07.510 align:start position:0%
the european parliament has condemned  russia's invasion of ukraine calling it  illegal unprovoked and unjustified  in their resolution voted at an  emergency session in brussels meps also  condemned the involvement of belarus  which has allowed russia to use its  territory as a staging post  the message from europe is clear  we will  stand up  we will not look away  when those fighting in the streets for  our values  face down putin's massive  war machine  we will support the international  criminal court's jurisdiction  and investigation of war crimes in  ukraine addressing the parliament via  video link from kiev the ukrainian  president welcomed eu help and called  for more support and more solidarity  since russia invaded on the 24th of  february the united nations says  hundreds of civilians have been killed  and hundreds of thousands  displaced men women children are dying  once again  because a foreign leader president putin  decided that their country ukraine has  no right to exist and we will never ever  let that happen and never ever accept  that  members expressed their solidarity with  ukrainians and welcomed the response of  ukraine's neighbors keeping their  borders open and helping refugees  they called for more protection for the  most vulnerable including women children  the sick and disabled  we are putting maximum pressure on  russia and its leaders we are stepping  up to support ukraine and the ukrainian  people  mep meps backed the eu's unprecedented  sanctions against the regime of vladimir  putin but said the eu needed to go  further restricting imports of oil and  gas  they expressed their support for the eu  providing lethal defensive equipment and  the banning of the kremlin-backed  propaganda channels rt and sputnik  parliament also called on eu  institutions to work towards granting  ukraine candidate status after its  request to join the european union
 

